|text=I was '''lovers''' with a woman I'll call Judy. One morning when we were sharing our dreams, I told her the dream I'd had where I was making an eloquent speech in Japan about saving the whales{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-02-17|author=Nan Alamilla Boyd|author2=Horacio N. Roque Ramirez|title=Bodies of Evidence: The Practice of Queer Oral History|publisher=OUP USA|isbn=9780199742738|page=209
|text=I was '''lovers''' with Joan — she was an artist for ONE Inc.}}
