|text=I was '''lovers''' with this boy in my neighborhood for... oh, I'd say at least eight years. And everybody in the neighborhood knew. And we came out that year.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2020-11-13|author=Marty Fink|title=Forget Burial: HIV Kinship, Disability, and Queer/Trans Narratives of Care|publisher=Rutgers University Press|isbn=9781978813762|page=82
|text=I was '''lovers''' with him, I think, either right before he'd had his diagnosis, or he'd already been diagnosed, and to me, it didn't matter.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2022-12-06|author=George Lakey|title=Dancing with History: A Life for Peace and Justice|publisher=Seven Stories Press|isbn=9781644212363
|text=I was '''lovers''' with a man. But in terms of the broader public, I was still in the closet.}}

